Certain items are already marked "special" so that the game is
winnable even if the player makes a mistake.  For instance, the Book
of the Dead and stuff can't be put into any bad, thus saving them from
the annoying "magical explosion".  And the Book doesn't burn too.
Ditto for the Amulet.  They won't polymorph either.

These are not logical, but they are essential to win the game.  In the
same light, I think the Oracle and the Quest leader shouldn't be
killable, at least not by the pet.  Having a polymorphed pet black
dragon following you down to the Oracle level is hardly the kind of
"mistake" that justifies the punishment.

Of course, the Oracle is not "essential" to win the game, since you
can always read spoilers or get extremely lucky in the sequence of
events, but the way the game is designed is supposed to be
self-contained.

I don't see anything wrong of my pet attacking my leader's minions or
a co-aligned priest.  That's what it takes to have a pet. :)

